        {
          "question": "window-near-endpoint",
          "status": "answered",
          "node": "a97A02:B1",
          "quote": "The reading is the zero\nextension: integrate against Lebesgue measure restricted to \\( [0,1] \\), so\nthe part of the window outside contributes nothing, which is exactly the\nintegral of the extended function, and the average is the window integral\ndivided by \\( 2h \\). Near an endpoint you are averaging over a shorter\neffective window, still dividing by \\( 2h \\).",
          "ink_words": 62,
          "graph_support": [
            {
              "graph": "holes/inkup/reasoning/a97A02-window-meaning.json",
              "edge": {
                "from": "restriction-warrant",
                "relation": "warrants",
                "to": "window-meaning"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "question": "continuity-from-integrability",
          "status": "answered",
          "node": "a97A02:B4",
          "quote": "Continuity of \\( f_h \\)\nfrom \\( f \\in L^{p} \\) then comes in two stages: first \\( f \\) is integrable,\nas in B2, and second the primitive lemma applies because the restricted\nLebesgue measure has no atoms, so \\( b \\mapsto \\int_{(-\\infty,b]} f \\) is\ncontinuous, and \\( t \\mapsto F(t\\pm h) \\) is continuous on \\( [0,1] \\).",
          "ink_words": 61,
          "graph_support": [
            {
              "graph": "holes/inkup/reasoning/a97A02-primitive-continuity.json",
              "edge": {
                "from": "primitive-warrant",
                "relation": "requires",
                "to": "integrable-f"
              }
            },
            {
              "graph": "holes/inkup/reasoning/a97A02-primitive-continuity.json",
              "edge": {
                "from": "primitive-warrant",
                "relation": "requires",
                "to": "no-atoms"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "question": "why-not-symmetric-difference",
          "status": "answered",
          "node": "a97A02:B4",
          "quote": "that estimate needs care: the difference has measure\n\\( 2\\min(\\lvert s-t\\rvert, 2h) \\), not the \\( 2\\lvert s-t\\rvert \\) one first\nwrites down, since once \\( \\lvert s-t\\rvert \\) exceeds \\( 2h \\) the windows\nare disjoint; the \\( L^{q} \\) bookkeeping degenerates at \\( q=\\infty \\); and\n\\( p=1 \\) needs a separate fallback through absolute continuity.",
          "ink_words": 58,
          "graph_support": [
            {
              "graph": "holes/inkup/reasoning/a97A02-why-primitives.json",
              "edge": {
                "from": "sd-bookkeeping",
                "relation": "resolved-by",
